        (10, "Explain how poverty and malnutrition reinforce each other and identify the interventions that can break the cycle.", "The loop is intergenerational and multi-causal, so the answer must trace deprivation through undernutrition, impaired development and low human capital back to low earnings, then attach named multi-sectoral levers rather than a single-scheme remedy.", [1, 12, 18, 2]),
        (10, "Elucidate why measured poverty and measured hunger can move in different directions.", "Different instruments measure different deprivations, so the answer must separate monetary poverty, multidimensional poverty and anthropometry, then separate availability, access, absorption and utilisation to locate where the divergence is produced.", [17, 2, 3, 16]),
